Input: {"question": "What sport is Paddy Ryan associated with?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d00", "start": 0, "end": 225, "text": "Paddy Ryan Paddy Ryan (15 March 1851 – 14 December 1900) was an Irish American boxer, and became his sport's world's heavyweight champion from May 30, 1880 when he won the title from Joe Goss until losing his title to John L."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d00", "start": 226, "end": 255, "text": "Sullivan on February 7, 1882."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d00", "start": 256, "end": 325, "text": "Paddy Ryan was born in Thurles, Tipperary, Ireland on March 14, 1851."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d00", "start": 326, "end": 435, "text": "After moving to America, he lived in the Troy, New York area and was consequently nicknamed the Trojan Giant."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d00", "start": 436, "end": 567, "text": "After opening a saloon in 1874, he caught the attention of the athletic director of Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute, Jim Killoran."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d00", "start": 568, "end": 587, "text": "Killoran supposedly"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d01", "start": 0, "end": 79, "text": "Paddy Ryan | Boxing Wiki | Fandom Start a Wiki Sign In Do n't have an account ?"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d01", "start": 80, "end": 637, "text": "Register Sign In Boxing Wiki Explore Main Page Discuss All Pages Community Interactive Maps Recent Blog Posts Wiki Content Recently Changed Pages Matthew O'Neil Everipedia Boxing Archives MTK Global On Everipedia Gennady Golovkin Errol Spence Roberto Durán James `` Buster '' Douglas Living people Stephanie Jaramillo Ricky Hatton Gene Fullmer Sumya A