Irish-American rugby union player who plays prop for Rugby United New York and the United States men's national team."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d03", "start": 213, "end": 315, "text": "Ryan previously played for the Austin Elite, the Newcastle Falcons, , London Welsh, and Rugby Viadana."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d03", "start": 316, "end": 388, "text": "Ryan also previously played for Munster Rugby's Munster A and U20 sides."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d03", "start": 389, "end": 478, "text": "Ryan was born in Chicago, Illinois, but raised in Ireland, the son of an American mother."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d03", "start": 479, "end": 563, "text": "Ryan, along with his older brothers, played rugby for Highfield RFC and Dolphin RFC."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d03", "start": 564, "end": 605, "text": "Ryan would later play for Munster Rugby's"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d04", "start": 0, "end": 243, "text": "Earl Patrick Freeman Earl Patrick Freeman (August 23, 1932 – December 28, 1989) was a Canadian professional wrestler, best known by his ring name Paddy Ryan, who competed in North American and international promotions during the 1950s and 60s."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d04", "start": 244, "end": 523, "text": "While competing in western Canada and the Pacific Northwest, Freeman was involved in memorable feuds with Lumberjack Luke, Ripper Collins and \"Crippler\" Ray Stevens as a mainstay of NWA All-Star Wrestling, Pacific Northwest Wrestling and Stampede Wrestling during the late 1970s."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d04", "start": 524, "end": 649, "text": "Born in Hamilton, Ontario, Freeman began wrestling professionally during the 1950s finding success in Germany as Bud Freeman."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d04", "start": 650, "end": 662, "text": "Competing in"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d05", "start": 0, "end": 43, "text": "for Victor Chandler , a British bookmaker ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d05", "start": 44, "end": 186, "text": "[ 31 ] In 2010 , 2012 , 2014 , 2016 and 2018 , McGuinness took part in the charity football match Soccer Aid , which raises money for Unicef ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d05", "start": 187, "end": 219, "text": "The match is aired live on ITV ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d05", "start": 220, "end": 280, "text": "In 2012 , McGuinness played Gary in Keith Lemon : The Film ."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d05", "start": 281, "end": 346, "text": "In 2013 , McGuinness joined Pizza Hut as their brand ambassador ."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d05", "start": 347, "end": 461, "text": "[ 32 ] In 2017 , McGuinness joined Jackpot Joy as their brand ambassador , taking over from Dame Barbara Windsor ."}, "D6S7": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d05", "start": 462, "end": 495, "text": "[ citation needed ] Personal life"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d00:c0", "entity": "Paddy Ryan", "scope": "sport", "claim": "Paddy Ryan is associated with boxing.", "answer": "boxing", "quote": "Paddy Ryan Paddy Ryan (15 March 1851 – 14 December 1900) was an Irish American boxer, and became his sport's world's heavyweight champion from May 30, 1880 when he won the title from Joe Goss until losing his title to John L.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0356-a0592c5bae4d:d01", "c